From: John Starks <jostarks@microsoft.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hv: mshv: keep GIC enabled by default for ARM64 partitions

The legacy create-partition ioctl disables every processor feature on
ARM64. Hyper-V requires GICv3/v4 for ARM64 child partitions, so creation
fails with EINVAL unless userspace supplies explicit feature banks.

Keep the required GIC feature enabled in the default mask, matching the
ARM64 default in mshv-ioctls. Explicit userspace feature banks still
override this default, and the x86_64 defaults are unchanged.

---
 drivers/hv/mshv_root_main.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/hv/mshv_root_main.c b/drivers/hv/mshv_root_main.c
--- a/drivers/hv/mshv_root_main.c
+++ b/drivers/hv/mshv_root_main.c
@@ -3162,5 +3162,8 @@ static long mshv_ioctl_process_pt_flags(void __user *user_arg, u64 *pt_flags,
 	disabled_xsave->xsave_comp_support = 0;
 	disabled_xsave->xsave_supervisor_support = 0;
+#elif IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ARM64)
+	/* GICv3/v4 is required for ARM64 child partitions. */
+	disabled_procs->gic_v3v4 = 0;
 #endif
 
 	/* Check if user provided newer struct with feature fields */
